From 0e558b86f3ef306b95dfbe8472aa93f3648d0b5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:52:25 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(news): open articles in Telegram Instant View when
 available
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

News cards on TeamPage and MatchDetail used <a target="_blank">, which
bounces the user out to a browser. Inside Telegram's WebView that means
leaving the mini app entirely — a hard exit from the shell.

Extract a shared NewsCard component and open articles via
WebApp.openLink(url, { try_instant_view: true }) when the Telegram SDK
is present (typed bridge: lib/telegram.ts grows openInTelegram, the
same fallback-shaped helper shareToTelegram already is). Telegram's
Instant View renders the article in an in-app reader when ESPN's page
supports it; otherwise it falls back to Telegram's in-app webview.
Outside Telegram the fallback is
window.open(url, "_blank", "noopener,noreferrer").

The card markup is now shared between TeamPage and MatchDetail, so the
two stay in sync and any future polish (share button, placeholders)
lands in one place.

