From 74514760bd1c12668ae9204b806dc57f1055b029 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:15:50 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(i18n): close the team-short-name and round-label
 translation gaps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Audited every team string the data layer can return for the five
synced leagues against teamNamesFa, straight out of the live DB after
a sync. Exactly one gap in the big five: ESPN's scoreboard shortName
for Manchester United is "Man Utd", while the dictionary only held
"Man United", so the lookup fell through and the English short name
rendered on the feed, the club header and the standings row. That was
the one English team name visible in FA — a Playwright pass over every
league tab confirmed the other four leagues are fully covered.

Round labels: roundFromEvent title-cases what it extracts, so it emits
"Round Of 16", not the "Round of 16" the dictionary keys on — a silent
case miss. Add the emitted casing, plus the round labels the Cups
grouping can show ("Group Stage", "League Phase", "Leg 1/2",
"Matchday", "Knockout Stage") and the unhyphenated Quarterfinal /
Semifinal spellings. Unknown rounds still pass through as ESPN's
English label rather than blanking.

Card meta ("GW N") needed no work: matches.cardMeta and table.gw were
already "{league} · هفته {gw}" and "{gw} هفته" in FA.

