Subject: [PATCH 3/3] polish(table): form reads as colored squares with
 letters, on the club page too
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The form column was five 6px dots — visually weak, and you had to
decode colours to know a club's run. Each result is now a 14px square
with a tinted fill, a 1px inset ring for definition on the dark
surface and the result letter inside: W/D/L in EN, ب/ت/خ in FA (the
first letter of each Persian word, same convention). The column goes
3rem → 5rem; the numeric columns and the row gap tighten one step to
pay for it, so the team-name cell GAINS room instead of losing it
(96px of text vs 92px before) — measured on a 390px phone, no name
truncates that didn't already, and neither the row nor the page scrolls
sideways.

The club page now carries the same strip in its header, folded on the
client from the same stored finished matches server/standings/form.ts
folds for the table, scoped to the club's own league so the two strips
can never disagree. The visible "Form" label is aria-hidden because the
strip already announces itself as a full sentence. MatchDetail's Form
tab picks the polish up for free — it renders the shared FormStrip.

Verified in headless Chrome, EN and FA: letters, inset rings, geometry
(no overflow, no clipped names) and the aria labels.

